 <class>WindowsStyleGesturesConfig</class>
 <widget class="QWidget" name="WindowsStyleGesturesConfig">
  <layout class="QFormLayout" name="formLayout">
   <item row="0" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="gesturesLabel">
     <property name="text">
      <string>Gestures:</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="0" column="1">
    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="kcfg_TaskSwitcherEnabled">
     <property name="text">
      <string>3-finger recents and 4-finger drag (requires InputActions)</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="1" column="1">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="taskSwitcherHint">
     <property name="text">
      <string>With InputActions installed (see the README), 3-finger up opens the task switcher and keeps it open until you lift. Left/right opens recents when closed and cycles through apps; after 300 ms it switches to the highlighted app. 3-finger down cancels recents or shows the desktop. A 4-finger swipe starts a sticky left-button drag: lift the fingers, continue with one finger, then tap once with one finger to drop. Turning this off suspends InputActions, restoring KDE's normal 3- and 4-finger gestures.</string>
     </property>
     <property name="wordWrap">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
  </layout>
 </widget>
